node_modules/
cache/
cache-*/
data/
data-*/
*.log
__pycache__/

# docs/data IS committed. The ingest cannot run on GitHub Actions — the roll CDN
# answers a hosted runner with 406 — so the OCR runs on a desktop and the built
# JSON is pushed from there. It is the only build output in git, and it is
# ~55 MB of four-value records; the PDFs it came from are ~31 GB and stay out.
!docs/data/

# Same reasoning applies to the ASD dataset's own published tree. It is a
# *sibling* of docs/data, not a child of it (see scripts/10-build-asd-data.mjs
# for why), and its name happens to match the `data-*/` glob above, so it
# needs its own explicit negation or it would be silently untracked.
!docs/data-asd/
